yoyo doctor now exits 1 when any row fails (✗) and 0 when every row passes or only warns. The REPL /doctor still doesn't exit. fmt, clippy and the full cargo test run all pass, and it's committed as Fixes #1244, so the push will close the ticket.

What I changed:
• Exit code: a new doctor_exit_code decides it, handle_doctor returns it, and the shell doctor arm in dispatch_sub.rs exits with it the way health does (+2 lines). dispatch.rs didn't need touching.
• Which rows can fail (beyond the ticket's minimum): before writing code I listed every row that could print ✗ and posted the table on #1244. Several would have broken CI for users whose setup is actually fine, so I changed them:
  • API key row: it was reporting false failures. It only checked one variable, so a Google user with only GEMINI_API_KEY set, or anyone using --api-key, API_KEY or the config file's api_key, saw "✗ not set" even though a run would find the key. It now checks the same key a run would use.
  • Git and project tools: these are now warnings, not failures. That covers git itself, Java/Maven/Gradle, Ruby/Bundler/Gem and CMake/Make/cc. A missing tool is often a normal setup (./gradlew, CMake with Ninja), and yoyo health already exits 1 on a real build failure.
  • API connection rows: these stay failures (refused key, unreachable endpoint, 404 and the rest), because the next run would fail the same way.
• Tests: in src/commands_dev_tests.rs, covering all-pass → 0, warn-only → 0, one fail → 1, plus a table for the API key row. Four integration tests had pinned exit 0 for a yoyo doctor with no key. Their env strips every key or points at a closed port, so each run really has a ✗ row; they now expect 1. None were deleted.
• Docs: the exit-code paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md now lists doctor next to health.

Checks on the built binary: all runs were in temp dirs and only touched 127.0.0.1:9 (a closed port) and a local Python stub, never a real host.
• Closed port with a fake key: exit 1.
• Stub with every row passing or warning: exit 0.
• Same, with git and cmake missing from PATH: those rows show ⚠ and the exit is 0.
• Google with only GEMINI_API_KEY set: the key row shows ✓ (the API row still fails against the closed port).

Recall controls: I disabled doctor_exit_code, and separately put the old API key logic back. Each time the matching test failed by name, and after restoring it passed again. I posted the results on #1244 before the full test run. The commit body has the row table, the probes and both controls.

commands_dev.rs is now at 1996 lines, just under the 2000-line module limit, so further changes there will need to go in a sibling file.
